Tonight, take a slow and relaxing journey through the human body while you drift toward sleep.

In this calming anatomy and physiology sleep documentary, we explore how the human body works from the surface of the skin to the tiny cells that make up every part of you. Discover how your skin protects and regulates your body, how living bones rebuild themselves, how muscles create movement, and how the heart continuously pumps blood through an extraordinary network of vessels.

We’ll gently travel through the lungs and discover how oxygen enters the bloodstream, follow food through the digestive system, explore the liver and kidneys, and learn how these organs quietly process nutrients, balance fluids, and remove waste.

The journey continues into the human brain, nervous system, senses, hormones, immune system, and finally the microscopic world of human cells — the building blocks behind everything your body does.

Designed for relaxation, sleep, and effortless learning, this slow-paced exploration of human anatomy requires nothing from you. There are no tests and nothing you need to memorize.

Simply get comfortable, close your eyes, and discover the remarkable systems keeping your body alive while you relax, unwind, and fall asleep.

