Why are you the way you are? This video takes a slow journey through the science of human personality—from ancient temperament theories to the modern Big Five traits.
We explore how genes and environment shape personality, what twin studies reveal, why situations can change how we behave, and how neuroscience, life experiences, relationships, and the stories we tell about ourselves all play a role. We also look at one of the biggest questions in personality psychology: can your personality actually change over time?

