What actually is an emotion, and why does your brain create feelings like fear, anger, sadness, excitement, or joy?

In this slow, relaxing journey through emotion science, we explore how our understanding of feelings evolved from ancient philosophy and Darwin to modern neuroscience. We look at basic emotion theory, the circumplex model, Lisa Feldman Barrett’s theory of constructed emotion, interoception, predictive processing, emotional regulation, and why emotions may have evolved to help us survive, make decisions, and connect with others.

Settle in and discover how the brain, body, past experience, and culture all come together to shape what you feel.

